       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled daily dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max dose.\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 1,700 mg/day total.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is a common regimen.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. I'd still advise against it."
      }
