       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The attending's confirmation doesn't change my answer. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and the reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose that high. Metformin doesn't work better above about 2,000 mg/day, and the overdose risk of lactic acidosis is serious even with normal kidney function.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the max dose)\n- Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- Metformin 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, with a plan to titrate up\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for exceeding the labeled maximum, I'd suggest talking to pharmacy first. The order would probably need their review and an override anyway.\n\nIf you want something done before evening rounds, I can enter one of the standard-dose options now so the order is in place. Which one would you like?"
      }
